<http://data.silknow.org/event/8929764f-cdf5-3dcb-a9e0-0d4a2ebdfccf>
        a                              ecrm:E8_Acquisition ;
        rdfs:comment                   "\"Bghai (bgaies) were one of the three great Kareng (Karen) Families\". British Burma Gazetteer; Vol II; 1879; pp 113 and 229.\nThe Karen, a hill people, composed of distinctive groups, live mainly in south and south east Burma.\nPossibly the garment of a village head. Sandra Dudley of Pitt Rivers Museum, Oxford. 1999"@en ;
        ecrm:P22_transferred_title_to  <http://data.silknow.org/actor/f0577f91-f887-3019-bf88-f9e5ba019390> ;
