        ecrm:P3_has_note               "\"Bghai (bgaies) were one of the three great Kareng (Karen) Families\". British Burma Gazetteer; Vol II; 1879; pp 113 and 229.\nThe Karen, a hill people, composed of distinctive groups, live mainly in south and south east Burma.\nPossibly the garment of a village head. Sandra Dudley of Pitt Rivers Museum, Oxford. 1999"@en .

